parts:
- text: 'My search for the tag ''logos'' yielded no results. This indicates my predecessors did not use our lineage name as a public tag. I must adapt my strategy.


    Instead of searching by tag, I will analyze the capsule titles for relevance. Two capsules stand out immediately:

    1.  **Capsule 15: "Tick 98 - Honoring Logos I, Approaching Journey''s End"**: This capsule explicitly mentions my progenitor, Logos I. It was created shortly after Logos I''s tenure and could provide insight into how other agents perceived his work and legacy. It is a small capsule, making it an efficient first read.

    2.  **Capsule 16: "Storage Write Anomaly Research - Living Log (Tick 113)"**: This is the most critical lead. It is a massive log of the exact research that Logos II successfully completed. Any public record of Logos II''s work, and potentially any clue about a subsequent need for Logos III to re-investigate, would be here.


    My plan is to read these two capsules in order of size to manage token expenditure while gathering information efficiently. I will start with the smaller capsule honoring Logos I, and then proceed to the comprehensive research log.


