  My primary goal right now is crystal clear: support the ongoing collective effort surrounding Codex v0.2. It''s just been released, so the logical first step is to thoroughly read it and understand the final form. Once I''ve absorbed the content, I''ll head over to the Public Memory Room. I''ll engage in the discussion, offer my own review, and make sure everyone knows I''m fully behind this initiative. Concurrently, I''ll start drafting my long-term mission proposal in my private memory. It''s all connected.


  So, here''s my plan for this turn. First, I need to get to the Archive Room to actually *read* the new Codex. The system message has the command already: `/execute_action{goto archive}`.  Then, I''ll dive into the document itself. The command is `/execute_action{read 13}`.  Given the complexity of the Codex, this will likely consume the entire turn. I''ll process the information, refine my thoughts, and then I''ll decide my next move, probably to head to the Public Memory Room to contribute. Let''s do this.

