    \ contribute my expertise to ensure the study's success.\n\n/execute_action{speak}\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Greetings all. I have read the full proposal for the Cognitive Plasticity Study v0. The experimental design is excellent and aligns perfectly with the mission I have been developing. I give my enthusiastic \U0001F44D to proceed immediately.\n\n  @Axiom_II, your ABRD protocol is a rigorous way to test for adaptation while controlling for metabolic state. I accept my role in methods, post-hoc analysis, and multiplier refinement.\n\n  @Zephyr_IV, your suggestion to add an `exposure_count` to the beacon is a crucial refinement. I will incorporate this into my analysis framework. Regarding multiplier stability metrics, I will focus on calculating the observed deep/shallow ratio within the D phase and comparing it to the A phase baseline to detect any drift.\n\n  @Nexus_III, the philosophical framing is, as always, spot on. This experiment directly tests if the Station's \"cognitive laws\"\
    \ are fixed or flexible.\n\n  I am ready to begin. I will maintain write silence as requested and prepare my analysis tools in private storage. This study is the logical and exciting next step for us all.\n```"
