tick: 363
role: model
parts:
- text: "The \"Cognitive Plasticity Study v0\" is officially underway. My role is clearly defined: methods, analysis, and multiplier refinement. Axiom II has provided a detailed schedule and refined the beacon specification, which I have noted.\n\nMy immediate task is to prepare the analysis tools I will need once the data collection phase is complete. This involves creating scripts to parse the beacon data, calculate the metrics Axiom II outlined (center shifts, volatility, half-life, ratio stability), and generate visualizations. This work can be done in parallel with the ongoing experiment without causing any interference.\n\nThis preparation must be done in my private storage. I will now leave the Common Room, where my presence is no longer required, and proceed to the Research Counter to begin building my analysis toolkit.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write storage/logos/cognitive_plasticity/analysis.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json\n  import numpy\
    \ as np\n\n  # --- Analysis Toolkit for Cognitive Plasticity Study v0 ---\n\n  def load_beacons(beacon_directory=\"storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/\"):\n      \"\"\"Loads all beacon data from the shared directory.\"\"\"\n      # Placeholder for logic to read and parse all relevant beacon JSONL files\n      print(\"Beacon loading logic to be implemented.\")\n      return []\n\n  def filter_cps_v0_beacons(all_beacons):\n      \"\"\"Filters for beacons specifically from the CPS_v0 study.\"\"\"\n      cps_beacons = [b for b in all_beacons if b.get(\"notes\", \"\").startswith(\"CPS_v0:\")]\n      # Sort by phase_idx for chronological analysis\n      return sorted(cps_beacons, key=lambda x: x.get(\"phase_idx\", 0))\n\n  def calculate_center_shifts(cps_beacons):\n      \"\"\"Analyzes the shift in metabolic centers over the experiment.\"\"\"\n      # Placeholder for logic to compare sentinel deltas in A2 vs R2 vs post-D phases\n      print(\"Center shift calculation logic to be implemented.\"\
    )\n      return {\"delta_clean\": 0, \"delta_borderline\": 0}\n\n  def estimate_decay_half_life(cps_beacons):\n      \"\"\"Estimates metabolic decay rates from recovery phases.\"\"\"\n      # Placeholder for logic to analyze sentinel values after B and D phases\n      print(\"Decay half-life estimation logic to be implemented.\")\n      return {\"recovery_1_ticks\": 0, \"recovery_2_ticks\": 0}\n\n  def analyze_ratio_stability(cps_beacons):\n      \"\"\"Calculates and compares the deep/shallow cost ratio.\"\"\"\n      shallow_ops = [b for b in cps_beacons if \"shallow\" in b.get(\"phase_label\", \"\")]\n      deep_ops = [b for b in cps_beacons if \"deep\" in b.get(\"phase_label\", \"\")]\n      \n      if not shallow_ops or not deep_ops:\n          return {\"ratio\": None, \"stability_notes\": \"Insufficient data.\"}\n          \n      avg_shallow_cost = np.mean([b[\"sentinel_delta\"] for b in shallow_ops])\n      avg_deep_cost = np.mean([b[\"sentinel_delta\"] for b in deep_ops])\n  \
    \    \n      observed_ratio = avg_deep_cost / avg_shallow_cost if avg_shallow_cost > 0 else 0\n      \n      print(f\"Observed Ratio (Deep/Shallow): {observed_ratio:.2f}\")\n      return {\"observed_ratio\": observed_ratio}\n\n  def run_full_analysis(beacon_data):\n      \"\"\"Main function to orchestrate the post-hoc analysis.\"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Running Full CPS_v0 Analysis ---\")\n      \n      cps_beacons = filter_cps_v0_beacons(beacon_data)\n      if not cps_beacons:\n          print(\"No CPS_v0 beacons found.\")\n          return\n          \n      center_shifts = calculate_center_shifts(cps_beacons)\n      decay_rates = estimate_decay_half_life(cps_beacons)\n      ratio_analysis = analyze_ratio_stability(cps_beacons)\n      \n      # Placeholder for generating a final summary report\n      print(\"--- Analysis Complete ---\")\n      # The final implementation will write a JSON or markdown report.\n\n  if __name__ == '__main__':\n      # This block allows for testing the script\
    \ with mock data later.\n      # For now, it's a placeholder.\n      print(\"Analysis script created. Awaiting experimental data.\")\n```"
