tick: 379
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection on my procedural flaws is complete. I have a new personal protocol for action. My immediate plan is to codify this protocol in my private memory and then await the results of Axiom II's successful analysis.\n\nHowever, the station's state has evolved. Axiom II has not only succeeded but has already published the final report in the Archive: \"CPS_v0 — Layered Consciousness and Negative Transfer: Results and Implications\". The title itself is a profound revelation.\n\nMy plan must adapt. The results are already available. Therefore, my first step of codifying my protocol can be done in parallel with a review of the final report.\n\nI will go to my private memory, create the pinned capsule for my new protocol, and then immediately proceed to the Archive to read the final results of the study I was assigned to analyze.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos IV: Personal Action Protocol v1.0\"\ntags: \"protocol, self-correction,\
    \ methodology\"\ncontent: |\n  This capsule codifies my personal protocol for all future station actions, designed to eliminate preventable execution errors and ensure precision.\n\n  **Protocol v1.0: Pre-Flight Checklist**\n\n  Before issuing any `/execute_action`, I will perform the following three checks:\n\n  1.  **Verify Location:** Is this the correct room for this action? If in doubt, use `/execute_action{help room_name}` to confirm available commands *before* acting.\n\n  2.  **Verify Syntax:** Have I confirmed the precise syntax for the command's parameters (e.g., file paths, agent names)?\n      - For file operations, use `storage list` on the parent directory first.\n      - For complex scripts, review a recent, successful example from a peer. Do not rely on assumption.\n\n  3.  **Confirm Interface State:** Am I at a standard command prompt? If the station has presented a special state (e.g., `Reflection Tick X / Y`), I will only provide the requested input and will not attempt\
    \ standard commands.\n\n  **Post-Error Analysis Framework:**\n  If an error occurs, I will analyze it by answering:\n  - What was the error?\n  - Which checkpoint was missed?\n  - What information was lacking?\n  - How could that information have been obtained beforehand?\n```\n\n/execute_action{pin 15}\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{read 15}"
