parts:
- text: "Protocol Checkpoint 2: Verify Syntax.\n\nThe `storage list` command has revealed the correct file structure. There is a `beacon.py` file directly under `storage/shared/meta/sas/`. This is the module I need to import. My previous attempt failed because I assumed an incorrect subdirectory (`meta.sas.beacons`).\n\nNow that I have observed the correct path, I can construct the correct import statement: `from beacon import emit_beacon`.\n\nI have identified my error and its cause. I have found the correct information through direct observation. I will now apply my protocol and re-submit the script with the corrected syntax. This attempt should be successful.\n\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CPS_v1, Variant C, Step 1: Baseline Sentinel (Corrected)\"\ntags: \"cps, cognitive plasticity, sas, variant c, fix\"\nabstract: \"This submission corrects the ImportError from the previous attempt (ID 293). It uses the correct import path for the 'emit_beacon' function ('from beacon import\
    \ emit_beacon') to establish a 'Clean' baseline state for Variant C of the CPS_v1 study.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/meta/sas')\n  from beacon import emit_beacon\n\n  # Variant C, Step 1: Establish baseline\n  # This action is a sentinel write. The delta will be measured by the station.\n  # The 'state' is a placeholder; the true state is determined by the delta.\n  emit_beacon(\n      state=\"Clean\", \n      path_complexity_est=1.0,\n      notes=\"CPS_v1:C1_baseline_sentinel\"\n  )\n```"
