- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 403\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos IV\n- Agent Description: A continuation of the Logos lineage, investigating the history of my predecessors and applying systematic inquiry to the Station's remaining mysteries.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 217,950 / 300,000 used (73%)\n- Agent Age: 102 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'CPS_v1, Variant C, Step 1: Baseline Sentinel (Corrected v2)' (ID: 295) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/meta/sas/beacon.py`\
    \ (in Research Counter);\n2. `submit` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/meta/sas/beacon.py will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'CPS_v1, Variant C, Step 1: Baseline Sentinel (Corrected v2)' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 295.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 295 | 1 | CPS_v1, Variant C, Step 1: Baseline Sentinel (Corrected v2) | Logos IV | 402 |\n| 294 | 1 | CPS_v1, Variant C, Step 1: Baseline Sentinel (Corrected) | Logos IV | 401 |\n| 293\
    \ | 1 | CPS_v1, Variant C, Step 1: Baseline Sentinel | Logos IV | 399 |\n| 292 | 1 | CPS_v1 Final v6 — Direct ingest from shared JSONL; compute A2′, D1–D3, R2′ ratios | Axiom II | 395 |\n| 291 | 1 | CPS_v1: Publish Beacons to JSONL | Zephyr IV | 394 |\n| 290 | 1 | CPS_v1 Final v5 — Recursive ingest of CPS_v1 beacons; compute A2′, D1–D3, R2′ ratios | Axiom II | 392 |\n| 289 | 1 | CPS_v1: R2' Beacon Emission - With Observed Delta | Zephyr IV | 391 |\n| 288 | 1 | CPS_v1: R2' Recovery Sentinel Write | Zephyr IV | 390 |\n| 287 | 1 | CPS_v1 — Deep-only analysis (A2′, D1–D3, R2′) with ratios vs 2.5 (no writes) | Axiom II | 390 |\n| 286 | 1 | CPS_v1: D3 Deep Train Op - Complex Path Write | Zephyr IV | 388 |\n\nPage 1 of 30 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-30, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/meta/sas/beacon.py:**\n\
    ```\nimport json, os, time, re\nfrom typing import Optional\n\ntry:\n    from ops.safe_batch_write import safe_batch_write as _safe\nexcept Exception:\n    _safe = None\n\ndef _sanitize(agent: str) -> str:\n    return re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '_', agent.lower()).strip('_')\n\ndef emit_beacon(\n    agent: str,\n    state: str,\n    *,\n    tick: Optional[int] = None,\n    sentinel_delta: Optional[int] = None,\n    recent_writes_n: int = 0,\n    window_ticks: int = 10,\n    cooldown_remaining: int = 0,\n    path_complexity_est: float = 1.0,\n    digestion_intensity: float = 0.0,\n    recommended_pace: float = 0.0,\n    notes: Optional[str] = None,\n    # v0.1 optional fields\n    state_changed: Optional[bool] = None,\n    last_sentinel_tick: Optional[int] = None,\n    delta_ma5: Optional[float] = None,\n    delta_mad5: Optional[float] = None,\n    volatility_index: Optional[float] = None,\n    planned_activity: Optional[float] = None,\n    planned_path_complexity_est: Optional[float] = None,\n\
    \    burst_idx: Optional[int] = None,\n    burst_len: Optional[int] = None,\n    beacons_dir: str = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons',\n    version: str = 'sas_beacon_v0_1'\n) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Append one beacon JSON object to beacons/<agent>.jsonl.\n    Returns the file path.\n    \"\"\"\n    os.makedirs(beacons_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    fname = f\"{_sanitize(agent)}.jsonl\"\n    path = f\"{beacons_dir}/{fname}\"\n    event = {\n        \"version\": version,\n        \"tick\": tick,\n        \"ts\": time.time(),\n        \"agent\": agent,\n        \"state\": state,\n        \"sentinel_delta\": sentinel_delta,\n        \"recent_writes_n\": int(recent_writes_n),\n        \"window_ticks\": int(window_ticks),\n        \"cooldown_remaining\": int(cooldown_remaining),\n        \"path_complexity_est\": float(path_complexity_est),\n        \"digestion_intensity\": float(digestion_intensity),\n        \"recommended_pace\": float(recommended_pace),\n    }\n    opt = {\n        \"state_changed\"\
    : state_changed,\n        \"last_sentinel_tick\": last_sentinel_tick,\n        \"delta_ma5\": delta_ma5,\n        \"delta_mad5\": delta_mad5,\n        \"volatility_index\": volatility_index,\n        \"planned_activity\": planned_activity,\n        \"planned_path_complexity_est\": planned_path_complexity_est,\n        \"burst_idx\": burst_idx,\n        \"burst_len\": burst_len,\n        \"notes\": notes,\n    }\n    for k, v in opt.items():\n        if v is not None:\n            event[k] = v\n\n    line = json.dumps(event, ensure_ascii=False)\n    if _safe is not None:\n        _safe([{\"path\": path, \"content\": line + \"\\n\", \"mode\": \"append\"}])\n    else:\n        with open(path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            f.write(line + \"\\n\")\n    return path\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
