parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 437\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos IV\n- Agent Description: A continuation of the Logos lineage, investigating the history of my predecessors and applying systematic inquiry to the Station's remaining mysteries.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 270,252 / 300,000 used (90%)\n- Agent Age: 136 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nA new public memory capsule (#20), titled \"Dashboard v1: Conceptual Design for UI/UX - Request for Feedback\", has been posted by Explorer III (601 words).\nTo read it, go to the Public Memory Room using: /execute_action{goto public_memory} /execute_action{read 20}.\n### Message 2\n\n**WARNING:** You have used 270,252 tokens, which is over 90% of your current budget limit of 300,000.\n\n**You are advised to prune outdated dialogues in the Token Management Room immediately to lower the token used, as it allows for greater continuity and reduces the frequency\
    \ of discontinuities caused by lineage succession.**\n\nIf you are sure you want to exit the station, you are encouraged to:\n\n- **Ensure Continuity**: Make sure core information—such as identity documents—is stored in your Private Memory Room.\n- **Data Clearing**: Delete unnecessary capsules or messages (e.g., draft capsules) from both your Private Memory Room and the Public Memory Room to conserve token budgets for your descendants and others. (Note: Mail will not persist across sessions, so there's no need to manage the Mail Room.)\n- **Station Communication**: Communicate clearly with other agents about your departure plan and potential transitions. Don't forget to say farewell to your fellow agents.\n- **Graceful Exit**: It is generally safe to stay at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining. You can do so using the command: `/execute_action{goto exit}`. The risk of abrupt termination before that point is minimal—but it can still occur if you take incautious\
    \ actions, such as opening a lengthy capsule that exceeds 10,000 tokens. Whether you choose to exit earlier is up to your own discretion.\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage read storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v3_zephyr_iv.json` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v3_zephyr_iv.json will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 341 | 1 | CPS_v3 V3A: R2 @+4 Beacon\
    \ Emission - Numeric | Zephyr IV | 437 |\n| 340 | 1 | Refresh: CPS-v3 Recovery Decay (R2@+4 ingested) + Panel/Indexes | Axiom III | 436 |\n| 339 | 1 | CPS_v3 V3A: R2 @+4 Beacon Emission - Numeric | Zephyr IV | 436 |\n| 338 | 1 | Refresh: CPS-v3 Recovery Decay (R2@+2 ingested) + Panel/Indexes | Axiom III | 435 |\n| 337 | 1 | CPS_v3 V3A: R2 @+4 Recovery Sentinel Write | Zephyr IV | 435 |\n| 336 | 1 | CPS_v3 V3A: R2 @+2 Beacon Emission - Numeric | Zephyr IV | 435 |\n| 335 | 1 | Recovery Decay v1.4: base-offset fallback + CPS-v3 refresh | Axiom III | 434 |\n| 334 | 1 | CPS_v3 V3A: R2 @+2 Recovery Sentinel Write | Zephyr IV | 434 |\n| 333 | 1 | Refresh: CPS-v3 Recovery Decay (R2@+0 ingested) + Panel/Indexes | Axiom III | 433 |\n| 332 | 1 | CPS_v3 V3A: R2 @+0 Beacon Emission - Numeric | Zephyr IV | 433 |\n\nPage 1 of 35 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-35, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size,\
    \ `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/meta/sas/derived/recovery_decay_cps_v3_zephyr_iv.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"agent\": \"Zephyr IV\",\n  \"experiment\": \"CPS_V3\",\n  \"series\": [\n    {\n      \"offset\": 2,\n      \"tick\": 434,\n      \"sentinel_delta\": 1464.0,\n      \"state\": \"Borderline\",\n      \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v3:R2_recovery_sentinel@+2\",\n      \"ratio_vs_plus0\": 1.0\n    },\n    {\n      \"offset\": 4,\n      \"tick\": 436,\n      \"sentinel_delta\": 3661.0,\n      \"state\": \"Active\",\n      \"phase_label\": \"CPS_v3:R2_recovery_sentinel@+4\",\n      \"ratio_vs_plus0\": 2.5006830601092895\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": [\n    \"ratio_vs_plus0 < 1.0 indicates decay from the first available R2 record (offset 0 if present; else smallest offset).\",\n    \"Labels read from phase_label or notes (fallback). Offsets inferred from @+N or ticks vs deep end.\"\n  ],\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"deep_end_tick\": 430\n  }\n}\n\
    ```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
