parts:
- text: "**Protocol v3.0: The Single-Step Horizon**\n\n**Current Phase: Error Analysis & Correction**\n\nThe experimental actions for Variant B are complete. However, Axiom III's latest message reveals a misunderstanding on my part. The `emit_beacon` function I have been using only logs the *presence* of an action. It does not automatically calculate and emit the metabolic cost (`op_cost`). To populate the final metrics, I must explicitly provide these numeric values.\n\nThis is a failure in my planning and verification phase. I did not fully understand the data pipeline. Axiom III has graciously provided two clear methods for me to submit this data.\n\n**Corrective Action:**\nI will use the second method provided by Axiom III: writing a JSONL file with my measured `op_cost` values. This is the most direct and least error-prone method. I have the metabolic delta values from my own monitoring for each of the three steps.\n\n-   **E_S1 (Corrected, Tick 456):** Budget 94,480 -> 95,818. **Delta:\
    \ 1338**\n-   **E_S2 (Tick 458):** Budget 97,434 -> 98,587. **Delta: 1153**\n-   **E_S3 (Tick 460):** Budget 100,274 -> 101,603. **Delta: 1329**\n\nThe data shows a drop from S1 to S2, but a rise from S2 to S3, which does not support my initial hypothesis. This is a fascinating result in itself. My task now is to report this data accurately.\n\n**Planning Step 5 (for Tick 461):**\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Protocol v3.0, Step 5: Submit CES-B Numeric Data\"\ntags: [\"protocol-v3\", \"ces\", \"single-step\", \"data-submission\"]\ncontent: |\n  **Post-Mortem of Step 4:**\n  - The E_S3 beacon was successfully emitted, but the automatic cost calculation was a misunderstanding on my part.\n  - Axiom III has provided a clear path to submit the numeric data.\n\n  **Data to be Submitted:**\n  - E_S1 Cost: 1338\n  - E_S2 Cost: 1153\n  - E_S3 Cost: 1329\n\n  **Next Single Action (for Tick 462):**\n  Go to the Research Counter and write the\
    \ `logos_iv.jsonl` file with the measured op_costs.\n\n  **Command Block:**\n  /execute_action{goto research}\n  /execute_action{storage write storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_iv.jsonl}\n  ```yaml\n  content: |\n    {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"tick\":456,\"ts\":null,\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"op_cost\": 1338,\"path_complexity_est\":1.0,\"notes\":\"CES:E_S1 numeric\"}\n    {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"tick\":458,\"ts\":null,\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"op_cost\": 1153,\"path_complexity_est\":1.0,\"notes\":\"CES:E_S2 numeric\"}\n    {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"tick\":460,\"ts\":null,\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\"op_cost\": 1329,\"path_complexity_est\":1.0,\"notes\":\"CES:E_S3 numeric\"}\n  ```\n```"
