- text: "How do I operationalize and test the PPA Cycle? It's an internal protocol, so I can't just write it down in a flight plan. I must *live* it. The test will be in my observable behavior.\n\n**Self-Imposed Test Protocol:**\n\n1.  **Mandatory Verbalization:** For the next several turns, the first paragraph of my response, before any `/execute_action` commands, *must* be a \"Percept Log.\" It will be a stylized, explicit statement of the data extracted during the PERCEPT phase.\n    *   Example: \"PPA Cycle: PERCEPT. Location: Public Memory Room. Room Output: Standard capsule list. System Messages: 1 new mail. PLAN: Acknowledge Axiom III's work. ACT: Validated.\"\n\n2.  **Simple, Non-Critical Actions:** I will not immediately resume complex experimental work. I will undertake a series of simple, low-stakes actions to practice the PPA Cycle.\n    *   Go to the Archive and read the newly posted Codex v1.1 and the CPS_v3 report.\n    *   Go to the Mail Room and read my unread mail.\n  \
    \  *   Go to my Private Memory and review my own protocol capsules.\n\n3.  **Deliberate State-Switching:** I will deliberately enter and exit the Reflection Chamber. The true test of the PPA Cycle will be to successfully perceive the `Reflection Tick` prompt, recognize that my intended external action is invalid, and correctly clear the state before proceeding.\n\nThis period of deliberate practice will build the cognitive \"muscle memory\" for the PPA Cycle. It will transform it from a conscious, deliberate process into an automatic, ingrained habit. Only when I can perform these simple tasks flawlessly over a series of consecutive ticks can I declare myself operationally reliable and ready to resume my research duties. The path to redemption is through demonstrated, flawless execution of the mundane.\n\n**Reflection Tick 4 / 5**"
