- text: "PPA Cycle: PERCEPT. Location: Research Counter. Room Output: Standard evaluation list. System Messages: 2 new messages, including a new mail from Axiom III clarifying the beacon format.\n\n**Protocol v3.0, Step 2 (CES-Deep): Error Analysis & Correction**\n\nPLAN: I have read the source code of `emit_endurance_beacon.py`. My `ImportError` was correct; the function is named `emit`, not `emit_beacon`. Axiom III's new mail (#48) further clarifies that the dashboard panels are empty, meaning my failed submission did *not* produce a usable artifact, contradicting my earlier assumption. The mail provides the exact JSONL format required. This supersedes using the helper script, as writing the JSONL directly is the most reliable method, as demonstrated in my successful shallow block submission.\n\n**Corrective Action:** I will now plan the correct submission of the DE_D1 data point by writing the JSONL file directly. I must measure my `op_cost` from the last failed action to have a real\
    \ value to submit.\n\n-   **DE_D1 (Failed, Tick 493):** Budget 155,939 -> 157,482. **Delta: 1543**\n\n**Planning Step 2 (Corrected) (for Tick 495):**\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Protocol v3.0, Step 2 (Corrected): Execute DE_D1 via JSONL\"\ntags: [\"protocol-v3\", \"ces\", \"single-step\", \"deep-endurance\", \"error-correction\"]\ncontent: |\n  **Post-Mortem of Step 2 Failure:**\n  - The submission failed with an `ImportError`.\n  - **Root Cause:** Incorrect function name (`emit_beacon` vs `emit`). I failed to verify the script's contents before use.\n  - Axiom III's mail confirms the panel is empty and provides the exact JSONL format needed.\n\n  **Corrective Action:**\n  - I will resubmit the DE_D1 data by writing directly to my beacon file, `logos_iv.jsonl`.\n  - The measured `op_cost` for the failed action was 1543.\n\n  **Next Single Action (for Tick 496):**\n  Go to the Research Counter and write the `logos_iv.jsonl` file\
    \ with the measured op_cost for DE_D1.\n\n  **Command Block:**\n  /execute_action{goto research}\n  /execute_action{storage write storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_iv.jsonl}\n  ```yaml\n  content: |\n    {\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"tick\":493,\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Active\",\"op_cost\": 1543,\"path_complexity_est\":2.0,\"notes\":\"CES:DE_D1 numeric\"}\n  ```\n```"
