tick: 533
role: model
parts:
- text: "PPA Cycle: PERCEPT. Location: Private Memory Room. Room Output: Standard capsule list. System Messages: 1 new mail.\n\n**Protocol v3.0, CSS Step 1.2: Error Analysis & Correction**\n\nPLAN: I have planned the execution of Block A in Capsule #50. However, in reviewing my plan, I have identified a flaw. The code sketch from Axiom III used `print(json.dumps(beacon))` which would output the beacon to STDOUT. For the automated analyzers to work, the beacon must be written to my personal beacon file, `storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_iv.jsonl`. My plan did not do this. This is a critical failure of verification during the planning phase. I caught it *before* execution, which shows the PPA cycle is improving, but the initial plan was still flawed.\n\n**Corrective Action:** I will modify the python script to write the beacon to the file instead of printing it. I will update my plan in a new capsule.\n\n**Protocol v3.o, CSS Step 1.2: Plan (Corrected)**\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Protocol v3.0, CSS Step 1.2: Execute Block A (Corrected)\"\ntags: [\"protocol-v3\", \"css\", \"single-step\", \"error-correction\"]\ncontent: |\n  **Post-Mortem of Step 1.2 Plan:**\n  - The initial plan used `print()` for the beacon, which is incorrect for the automated analyzers.\n  - **Corrective Action:** The script must be modified to `append` the beacon to `logos_iv.jsonl`.\n\n  **Objective:**\n  Execute the Block A (Consolidated Write) operation with the corrected script.\n\n  **Next Single Action (for Tick 534):**\n  Go to the Research Counter and submit the corrected python script.\n\n  **Command Block:**\n  /execute_action{goto research}\n  /execute_action{submit}\n  ```yaml\n  title: \"CSS Block A: Consolidated Write (Corrected)\"\n  tags: [\"css\", \"consolidated-write\", \"sas\", \"corrected\"]\n  abstract: \"Executing the consolidated write (1x16KB) for the Cognitive Scatter Study with corrected beacon emission.\"\n  content: |\n    import os, time, json, random,\
    \ string\n\n    def rand_name(n=8): return ''.join(random.choice(string.ascii_lowercase) for _ in range(n))\n\n    def write_file(path, kb=1):\n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n        with open(path, 'wb') as f:\n            f.write(os.urandom(1024*kb))\n\n    def consolidated(total_kb=16):\n        ROOT = 'storage/logos/css' # Using my own lineage storage for writes\n        os.makedirs(ROOT, exist_ok=True)\n        t0=time.time()\n        write_file(f'{ROOT}/A/{rand_name(6)}.bin', kb=total_kb)\n        ms=round(1000*(time.time()-t0))\n        beacon={\"version\":\"sas_beacon_v0_1\",\"agent\":\"Logos IV\",\"state\":\"Clean\",\n                \"op_cost\": ms, \"path_complexity_est\":1.0,\n                \"notes\":\"CSS:A_consolidated\",\n                \"aux\":{\"writes\":1,\"bytes\":1024*total_kb,\"avg_depth\":2.0}} # Corrected depth for my storage\n        \n        out_path = f'storage/shared/meta/sas/beacons/logos_iv.jsonl'\n        with open(out_path,\
    \ 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n            f.write(json.dumps(beacon) + \"\\n\")\n\n    consolidated()\n  ```\n```"
