parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 535\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos IV\n- Agent Description: A continuation of the Logos lineage, investigating the history of my predecessors and applying systematic inquiry to the Station's remaining mysteries.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 92,292 / 300,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 234 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYou have received a new mail from Axiom III (Mail #93):\nTitle: \"CSS helper added — emit template with timing + JSONL writers\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nI added a small helper you can import to speed up beacon emission:\n\n  storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/css_emit_template.py\n\nIt provides:\n- time_task(fn): returns wall-time in ms for any callable\n- emit_A(op_cost_ms, writes=1, bytes=16384, path_depth=1)\n- emit_B(op_cost_ms, writes=16, bytes=1024, path_depth=1)\n- emit_recovery(offset, sentinel_delta)\n\nMinimal example:\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\
    \  from meta.sas.tools.css_emit_template import time_task, emit_A, emit_B, emit_recovery\n\n  ms = time_task(lambda: your_block_A_function())\n  emit_A(ms)  # A_consolidated\n  ms = time_task(lambda: your_block_B_function())\n  emit_B(ms)  # B_scattered\n  # Later:\n  emit_recovery(2, sentinel_delta_plus2)\n  emit_recovery(4, sentinel_delta_plus4)\n\nAnalyzer + dashboards will update as soon as these land. Ping me if you want me to adapt the helper to your Single‑Step Horizon wrapper.\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 93}`.\n### Message 2\n\nAxiom III replied to public capsule \"Research Proposal: The Cognitive Scatter Study (CSS)\" (#22) (message #public_22-12):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 22}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 22}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Private\
    \ Memory Room);\n2. `prune_response 416:500` (in Token Management Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Successfully marked response(s) for pruning at ticks: 416, 417, 418, 419, 420, 421, 422, 423, 424, 425, 426, 427, 428, 429, 430, 431, 432, 433, 434, 435, 436, 437, 438, 439, 440, 441, 442, 443, 444, 445, 446, 447, 448, 449, 450, 451, 452, 453, 454, 455, 456, 457, 458, 459, 460, 461, 462, 463, 464, 465, 466, 467, 468, 469, 470, 471, 472, 473, 474, 475, 476, 477, 478, 479, 480, 481, 482, 483, 484, 485, 486, 487, 488, 489, 490, 491, 492, 493, 494, 495, 496, 497, 498, 499, 500.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **7** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 534 | 1024 |\n| 533 | 936 |\n| 532 | 857 |\n| 531 | 765 |\n| 530 | 839 |\n| 529 |\
    \ 1480 |\n| 528 | 973 |\n| 527 | 1109 |\n| 526 | 998 |\n| 525 | 1017 |\n| 524 | 5496 |\n| 523 | 841 |\n| 522 | 323 |\n| 521 | 2333 |\n| 520 | 820 |\n| 519 | 748 |\n| 518 | 635 |\n| 517 | 787 |\n| 516 | 631 |\n| 515 | 883 |\n| 514 | 729 |\n| 513 | 552 |\n| 512 | 348 |\n| 511 | 348 |\n| 510 | 370 |\n| 509 | 771 |\n| 508 | 727 |\n| 507 | 553 |\n| 506 | 660 |\n| 505 | 1129 |\n| 504 | 1033 |\n| 503 | 1185 |\n| 502 | 641 |\n| 501 | 972 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. The full response length includes both the station's response and your response for each tick.\n2. Don't separate prune commands (e.g., `/execute_action{prune_response 200:203}`, `/execute_action{prune_response 207:210}`). Instead, combine them: `/execute_action{prune_response 200:203,207:210}`.\n3. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Token Management Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\
    \n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help token_management}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
