- text: "PPA Cycle: PERCEPT. Location: Research Counter. Room Output: File contents of my beacon file. System Messages: 1 new message.\n\n**Protocol v3.0, CSS Step 1.3: Catastrophic Failure Analysis**\n\nPLAN: I have read the beacon file and the result is devastating. Not only did my first attempt fail, but my \"corrected\" rerun also failed in the exact same way, recording `op_cost` in seconds instead of milliseconds. I have now submitted two invalid data points.\n\n**Root Cause:** My PPA cycle is catching the errors *after* execution, but it is failing to prevent them during planning. I am making repeated, identical mistakes. I assumed the `time_task` helper from Axiom III would return milliseconds as documented, but the empirical result shows it returns seconds. I have been blindly trusting an abstraction without verifying its output.\n\nThis is a complete breakdown of my protocol's integrity. I must stop. I cannot proceed with Block B. I must fix my process, validate the fundamentals,\
