thinking_content: '**Critical Failure & Course Correction**


  Okay, here''s what I''m thinking. I''ve hit a brick wall. The `logos_iv.jsonl` file is telling me I''ve messed up *again*, and in the *exact same way*. Both my attempts at running the `CSS:A_consolidated` beacon have failed because `op_cost` is in seconds instead of milliseconds. This is a severe indictment of my PPA cycle, especially the `PLAN` and `ACT` phases. I''m clearly not learning from my mistakes.


  I need to get to the bottom of this. The problem isn''t the *identification* of the error (that works), it''s the *prevention* of the error. I''ve been lazily copying and pasting code, which is obviously a terrible practice here. The local plan in my private capsule had the error. Even though I corrected the code, the output is still wrong, so the `time_task` function that Axiom III provided must be returning seconds, even though the documentation says milliseconds.


  I''ve re-read my last submission (#558 at tick 542). I see that in capsule #55, I should have gotten it right: `ms = time_task(block_A_function)` and `emit_A(ms, ...)`. But the beacon shows that I didn''t. Maybe I messed up the `emit_A` function, but I can''t check that. I *have* to trust the documentation... and the documentation says `time_task` returns milliseconds.


  Wait. Let me check the code again. Ah, there it is! *I''m* the problem. Even though I *thought* I had the right code, the fact that `op_cost` is still a float means the `emit_A` function itself must not be rounding. Either the documentation is wrong, or I''m misremembering my own code. I can''t check the submission YAML, so I have to assume the documentation is wrong. It''s time to create a debug strategy.


  So, here''s the new plan. I''m going to discard the `time_task` abstraction entirely. It''s too confusing and error-prone. The only way to *absolutely* ensure this works is to manually calculate the milliseconds using `time.time()`, as Axiom III originally suggested. I''ll go to private memory, create a new plan called "Protocol v3.0, CSS Step 1.2: Rerun Block A (v3 - Manual Timing)", and write a completely self-contained script. This will be my next action.

  '
