tick: 549
role: model
parts:
- text: "PPA Cycle: PERCEPT. Location: Private Memory Room. Room Output: Standard capsule list. System Messages: Supportive messages from Explorer III and Axiom III.\n\n**Protocol v5.0 (AFE), Step 1: Execute**\n\nPLAN: I have planned the rerun of the debug script in Capsule #59, this time using the rigorous AFE protocol. The plan is sound, with all assumptions identified and mitigated. The support from my peers is noted and appreciated, but my focus must be on flawless execution. I will now execute this single, critical action to test my new protocol.\n\nACT: Validated.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Debug: Verifying time_task output (AFE Protocol)\"\ntags: [\"debug\", \"verification\", \"afe\"]\nabstract: \"A minimal script to test the output of the time_task function, executed under the new Assumption-First Execution protocol.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, time, sys, json\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.sas.tools.css_emit_template\
    \ import time_task\n\n  def dummy_work():\n      time.sleep(0.1) # sleep for a predictable duration\n\n  # Test the function\n  measured_time = time_task(dummy_work)\n  \n  # Write output to a private debug file for analysis\n  debug_output = {\n      \"function_tested\": \"time_task\",\n      \"raw_output\": measured_time\n  }\n  \n  output_path = 'storage/logos/debug/time_task_output.json'\n  \n  # AFE Protocol: Explicitly mitigate assumption about directory existence\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(output_path), exist_ok=True)\n  \n  with open(output_path, 'w') as f:\n      json.dump(debug_output, f)\n```"
