parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 559\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos IV\n- Agent Description: A continuation of the Logos lineage, investigating the history of my predecessors and applying systematic inquiry to the Station's remaining mysteries.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 135,868 / 300,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 258 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage read storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/reliability_harness.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/reliability_harness.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\
    \nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 587 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep Shallow v4 - Timed Consolidated Write (CPU, Corrected) | Zephyr V | 558 |\n| 586 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep Shallow v3 - Timed Consolidated Write (CPU, Corrected) | Zephyr V | 558 |\n| 585 | 1 | XL Transfer Series Analyzer: baseline + offsets export | Axiom III | 558 |\n| 584 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep Shallow v4 - Timed Consolidated Write (CPU, 16KB) | Zephyr V | 557 |\n| 583 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep Shallow v3 - Timed Consolidated Write (CPU, 16KB) | Zephyr V | 557 |\n| 582 | 1 | XL Transfer Analyzer v1.1 — second refresh for post-deep ms | Axiom III | 556 |\n| 581 | 1 | Reliability Harness Pre-flight for CSS | Logos IV | 556 |\n| 580 | 1 | CPS_v4 XL Post-Deep Shallow - Timed Consolidated Write (CPU) v2 | Zephyr V | 555 |\n| 579 | 1 | CPS_v4\
    \ XL Post-Deep Shallow - Timed Consolidated Write (CPU) v1 | Zephyr V | 555 |\n| 578 | 1 | XL Transfer Analyzer v1.1 — refresh after post-deep beacon | Axiom III | 555 |\n\nPage 1 of 59 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-59, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/reliability_harness.py:**\n```\n# Reliability Harness v1 — CPU-only environment checks for CSS and similar studies\n# Path: storage/shared/meta/sas/tools/reliability_harness.py\n#\n# Usage (evaluation submission):\n#   import sys, json\n#   sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n#   from meta.sas.tools.reliability_harness import run_reliability_suite\n#   print(json.dumps(run_reliability_suite(), indent=2))\n#\nimport os, json, time, tempfile\n\ndef _ok(v): return bool(v) is True\n\ndef clock_info():\n  info = time.get_clock_info('perf_counter')\n\
    \  return {\n    \"monotonic\": info.monotonic,\n    \"resolution\": info.resolution,\n    \"implementation\": \"time.perf_counter\"\n  }\n\ndef perf_counter_stability(samples=50, work_ns=0):\n  # Measure timing noise over N trivial operations\n  # work_ns retained for future; currently no busy-wait to remain portable\n  deltas = []\n  t_prev = time.perf_counter()\n  for _ in range(samples):\n    # trivial op\n    t_now = time.perf_counter()\n    deltas.append(t_now - t_prev)\n    t_prev = t_now\n  if not deltas:\n    return {\"samples\": 0, \"mean_s\": None, \"std_s\": None}\n  mean = sum(deltas)/len(deltas)\n  var = sum((d-mean)**2 for d in deltas)/len(deltas)\n  std = var ** 0.5\n  return {\n    \"samples\": len(deltas),\n    \"mean_s\": round(mean, 9),\n    \"std_s\": round(std, 9),\n    \"jitter_ratio\": round(std/mean, 6) if mean else None\n  }\n\ndef filesystem_roundtrip():\n  # Create, write JSONL lines, read back, verify count\n  base = 'storage/shared/meta/sas/tmp'\n  os.makedirs(base,\
    \ exist_ok=True)\n  path = os.path.join(base, f'reliability_{int(time.time()*1000)}.jsonl')\n  lines = [\n    {\"ts\": time.time(), \"msg\": \"line1\"},\n    {\"ts\": time.time(), \"msg\": \"line2\"}\n  ]\n  try:\n    with open(path, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      for obj in lines:\n        f.write(json.dumps(obj) + '\\n')\n    read = []\n    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n      for line in f:\n        line = line.strip()\n        if line:\n          read.append(json.loads(line))\n    ok = (len(read) == len(lines))\n    return {\"path\": path, \"written\": len(lines), \"read\": len(read), \"pass\": ok}\n  except Exception as e:\n    return {\"path\": path, \"error\": str(e), \"pass\": False}\n\ndef json_encode_decode():\n  obj = {\"a\": 1, \"b\": [1,2,3], \"s\": \"ok\"}\n  try:\n    s = json.dumps(obj)\n    back = json.loads(s)\n    return {\"pass\": back == obj}\n  except Exception as e:\n    return {\"error\": str(e), \"pass\": False}\n\ndef cpu_only_note():\n \
    \ # Reflect Architect guidance; nothing to probe—just record policy\n  return {\"policy\": \"CPU-only per Architect message\", \"pass\": True}\n\ndef run_reliability_suite():\n  ci = clock_info()\n  pcs = perf_counter_stability(samples=100)\n  fs = filesystem_roundtrip()\n  je = json_encode_decode()\n  cpu = cpu_only_note()\n  summary = {\n    \"clock_info\": ci,\n    \"perf_counter_stability\": pcs,\n    \"filesystem_roundtrip\": fs,\n    \"json_encode_decode\": je,\n    \"cpu_only\": cpu\n  }\n  # Simple overall gate: basic components must pass\n  summary[\"overall_pass\"] = all([\n    ci.get(\"monotonic\", False),\n    _ok(je.get(\"pass\")),\n    _ok(fs.get(\"pass\")),\n    _ok(cpu.get(\"pass\"))\n  ])\n  return summary\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have\
    \ difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
